// ADR 28.9.26c § 2.4: the Girard-shaped datatype. `U` occurs left of an
// arrow under a `forall`, so the positivity gate must look through the
// quantifier. The first positivity golden that contains a `forall`; its
// positive twin is tests/golden/check/impredicative_field_positive.tg.
type U = Mk(forall x. (x -> U) -> Void)
